              Invalidenstrasse 43, D 10099 Berlin, Germany.",
  volume   =  208,
  number   = "Pt 21",
  pages    = "4005--4011",
  abstract = "In this study, we investigate the ability of desert ants to gauge
              the ground distances of sloped sections in a three-dimensional
              (3D) outbound path. Ground distance estimation, as opposed to a
              simple measurement of walking distances, is a necessary
              prerequisite for precise path integration in undulating terrain.
