              tilted floor would transect several layers of this putative
              lattice, resulting in interruption of the hexagonal pattern. We
              model this prediction with simulated grid lattices, and show that
              the firing of a grid cell on a 40$ ^\circ$-tilted surface should
              cover proportionally less of the surface, with smaller field size,
              fewer fields, and reduced hexagonal symmetry. However, recording
              of real grid cells as animals foraged on a 40$ ^\circ$-tilted
