  number   =  7872,
  pages    = "404--409",
  abstract = "As animals navigate on a two-dimensional surface, neurons in the
              medial entorhinal cortex (MEC) known as grid cells are activated
              when the animal passes through multiple locations (firing fields)
              arranged in a hexagonal lattice that tiles the locomotion
