  pages    = "13773--13778",
  abstract = "Biological networks have an inherent simplicity: they are modular
              with a design that can be separated into units that perform almost
              independently. Furthermore, they show reuse of recurring patterns
              termed network motifs. Little is known about the evolutionary
              origin of these properties. Current models of biological evolution
              typically produce networks that are highly nonmodular and lack
