  journal  = "Nat. Commun.",
  volume   =  12,
  number   =  1,
  pages    =  2392,
  abstract = "Cognitive maps are mental representations of spatial and
              conceptual relationships in an environment, and are critical for
              flexible behavior. To form these abstract maps, the hippocampus
              has to learn to separate or merge aliased observations
              appropriately in different contexts in a manner that enables
