              one-item fixed-capacity memory model, other monkey memory tests
              with four-item lists have shown performance impossible to obtain
              with a one-item capacity [7]. We suggest that this contradiction
              can be resolved using a continuous-resource approach more closely
              tied to the neural basis of memory [8, 9]. In this view, items
