  volume   =  462,
  number   =  7271,
  pages    = "353--357",
  abstract = "Gamma oscillations are thought to transiently link distributed
              cell assemblies that are processing related information, a
              function that is probably important for network processes such as
              perception, attentional selection and memory. This 'binding'
              mechanism requires that spatially distributed cells fire together
