              gamma oscillations varies substantially across space and time,
              from approximately 25 to almost 150 Hz. Here we show that gamma
              oscillations in the CA1 area of the hippocampus split into
              distinct fast and slow frequency components that differentially
              couple CA1 to inputs from the medial entorhinal cortex, an area
