              the mutual information of the system. Our analysis provides an
              estimate of the effective number of statistically independent
              degrees of freedom, denoted N(eff), that a large correlated system
              can have. According to our theory N(eff) remains finite in the
              limit of a large N. Estimating the parameters of the correlations
              and tuning curves from experimental data in some cortical areas
