              responses to repeated stimuli were reproducible, whereas the
              responses evoked by nonrepeated stimuli drawn from the same
              ensemble were variable. Stimulus-dependent information was
              quantified directly from the difference in entropy of these neural
              responses. We show that a single LGN cell can encode much more
