  volume   =  86,
  number   =  4,
  pages    = "2029--2040",
  abstract = "The superficial layers of the entorhinal cortex (EC) provide the
              majority of the neocortical input to the hippocampus, and the deep
              layers of the EC receive the majority of neocortically bound
              hippocampal outputs. To characterize information transmission
              through the hippocampal and EC circuitry, we recorded
