              an 18 m long linear track. The recordings spanned a range of more
              than 3 mm, covering approximately three quarters of the
              dorsoventral extent of the medial entorhinal cortex. Distinct
              periodic firing fields were observed at all recording levels. The
              average interpeak distance between the fields increased from
              approximately 50 cm in the most dorsal part to approximately 3 m
              at the most ventral recording positions. The increase in grid
              scale was accompanied by a decrease in the frequency of theta
