  volume   =  2,
  pages    =  8,
  abstract = "Inhibitory circuits in the brain rely on GABA-releasing
              interneurons. For long, inhibitory circuits were considered weakly
              plastic in the face of patterns of neuronal activity that trigger
              long-term changes in the synapses between excitatory principal
              cells. Recent studies however have shown that GABAergic circuits
