  volume   =  32,
  pages    = "435--506",
  abstract = "Since the work of Golgi and Cajal, light microscopy has remained a
              key tool for neuroscientists to observe cellular properties.
              Ongoing advances have enabled new experimental capabilities using
              light to inspect the nervous system across multiple spatial
              scales, including ultrastructural scales finer than the optical
