  volume   =  107,
  number   =  17,
  pages    = "7957--7962",
  abstract = "Driven either by external landmarks or by internal dynamics,
              hippocampal neurons form sequences of cell assemblies. The
              coordinated firing of these active cells is organized by the
              prominent ``theta'' oscillations in the local field potential
              (LFP): place cells discharge at progressively earlier theta phases
