  abstract = "Nitric oxide (NO.) does not react significantly with thiol groups
              under physiological conditions, whereas a variety of endogenous NO
              donor molecules facilitate rapid transfer to thiol of nitrosonium
              ion (NO+, with one less electron than NO.). Here, nitrosonium
