  volume   =  28,
  number   =  1,
  pages    = "30--42",
  abstract = "The mismatch negativity (MMN) is an event-related brain potential
              elicited by infrequent, physically deviant sounds in a sequence of
              repetitive auditory stimuli. Two dichotic listening experiments
              that were designed to optimize the selective focusing of attention
              provided a strong test of Naatanen's proposal that the MMN is
