              location. The adaptation field, estimated as the region of visual
              space where conditioning motion caused adaptation, was always
              larger than the MT receptive field. Use of the same stimulus
              configuration while recording from direction-selective neurons in
              V1 failed to demonstrate either adaptation or the
              transient-sustained response pattern that is the signature of
              short-term adaptation in MT. We conclude that the shift from
              transient to sustained firing in MT cells does not result from an
