  pages    = "311--322",
  abstract = "Gamma frequency oscillations (30-100 Hz) have been suggested to
              underlie various cognitive and motor functions. Here, we examine
              the generation of gamma oscillation currents in the hippocampus,
              using two-dimensional, 96-site silicon probes. Two gamma
              generators were identified, one in the dentate gyrus and another
              in the CA3-CA1 regions. The coupling strength between the two
              oscillators varied during both theta and nontheta states. Both
