  volume   =  65,
  number   = "5 Pt 1",
  pages    =  051922,
  abstract = "Neural networks with recurrent connections are sometimes regarded
              as too slow at computation to serve as models of the brain. Here
              we analytically study a counterexample, a network consisting of N
              integrate-and-fire neurons with self excitation, all-to-all
              inhibition, instantaneous synaptic coupling, and constant external
