              enough, the network performs a winner-take-all computation for all
              possible external inputs and initial states of the network. The
              computation is done very quickly: As soon as the winner spikes
              once, the computation is completed since no other neurons will
              spike. For some initial states, the winner is the first neuron to
              spike, and the computation is done at the first spike of the
              network. In general, there are M potential winners, corresponding
