              that the pulse exerts a weaker influence on LIP neuronal responses
              when the pulse is late relative to motion stimulus onset. We show
              that this violation of time-shift invariance (TSI) is consistent
              with a recurrent circuit mechanism of time integration. We further
              examine time integration using two consecutive pulses of the same
              or opposite motion directions. The induced changes in the
