  volume   =  22,
  number   =  22,
  pages    = "10053--10065",
  abstract = "The responses of neurons in the primary visual cortex (V1) are
              suppressed by mask stimuli that do not elicit responses if
              presented alone. This suppression is widely believed to be
              mediated by intracortical inhibition. As an alternative, we
              propose that it can be explained by thalamocortical synaptic
              depression. This explanation correctly predicts that suppression
              is monocular, immune to cortical adaptation, and occurs for mask
