              of basal ganglia function. We review the implications of these new
              models for a general understanding of basal ganglia function in
              normal as well as in diseased brains. The focus is on their
              functional similarities rather than on the details of mathematical
              methodologies and simulation techniques. Most of the models
              suggest a vital role for the basal ganglia in learning. Although
              this interest in learning is partly driven by experimental results
