  number   =  9,
  pages    = "1498--1530",
  abstract = "Synthetic neural modeling is a multilevel theoretical approach to
              the problem of understanding the neuronal bases of adaptive
              behavior. It uses simultaneous large-scale computer simulations of
              the nervous system, the phenotype, and the environment of a
              particular organism to study events and their interactions at
