  journal  = "Front. Neural Circuits",
  volume   =  6,
  pages    =  6,
  abstract = "When rodents engage in irregular foraging in an open-field
              environment, hippocampal principal cells exhibit place-specific
              firing that is statistically independent of the direction of
              traverse through the place field. When the path is restricted to a
              track, however, in-field rates differ substantially in opposite
