              observations on deefferented primary and secondary endings. The
              model can be used to predict responses to length changes of
              arbitrary time course. 3. Predicted responses to large
              ramp-and-hold stretch are quantitatively comparable to
              observations over a wide range of stretch velocities. The
              quantities compared include the increment in response during ramp
              stretch as well as the dynamic index, which is a measure of
              adaptation at stretch plateau. 4. At a fixed frequency of
