              functional roles of diverse cell types in movement-related areas
              of primate cortex. The model circuit maintains accurate
              proprioception while controlling voluntary reaches to spatial
              targets, exertion of force against obstacles, posture maintenance
              despite perturbations, compliance with an imposed movement, and
              static and inertial load compensations. Computer simulations show
