  journal  = "Science",
  volume   =  293,
  number   =  5536,
  pages    = "1845--1848",
  abstract = "For goal-directed arm movements, the nervous system generates a
              sequence of motor commands that bring the arm toward the target.
              Control of the octopus arm is especially complex because the arm
              can be moved in any direction, with a virtually infinite number of
