  author   = "Schmitt, J and Holmes, P",
  journal  = "Biol. Cybern.",
  volume   =  83,
  number   =  6,
  pages    = "501--515",
  abstract = "We study the dynamics and stability of legged locomotion in the
              horizontal plane. Motivated by experimental studies of insects, we
              develop two- and three-degree-of freedom rigid body models with
              pairs of 'virtual' elastic legs in intermittent contact with the
              ground. We focus on conservative compliant-legged models, but we
