              associated with larger steps recurring with the same repetition
              rate as the small steps of slow voluntary ramps. Maximal step
              amplitude observed was more than one order of magnitude larger
              than physiological tremor. 4. The individual 8-10 Hz cycle was
              asymmetrical in that decelerations usually reached higher peaks
              than the preceding acceleration, suggesting that the antagonist
              contributed with a braking action. Moreover, in very slow
