  number   = "Pt 3",
  pages    = "379--389",
  abstract = "The individual muscles of a multiple muscle group at a given joint
              are often assumed to function synergistically to share the load
              during locomotion. We examined two leg extensors of a running
              cockroach to test the hypothesis that leg muscles within an
              anatomical muscle group necessarily manage (i.e. produce, store,
