  author   = "Drew, Trevor and Jiang, Wan and Kably, Bouchra and Lavoie, Sylvain",
  journal  = "Can. J. Physiol. Pharmacol.",
  volume   =  74,
  number   =  4,
  pages    = "426--442",
  abstract = "One important aspect of locomotor control is the ability of an
              animal to make anticipatory gait modifications to avoid obstacles,
              by stepping either around them or over them. This paper reviews
              some of the evidence that suggests that the motor cortex is one of
              the principal structures involved in the control of such
              anticipatory gait modifications in cats, in particular when they
