  volume    =  2,
  pages     = "1--51",
  abstract  = "The effectiveness of connectionist models in emulating
               intelligent behaviour and solving significant practical problems
               is strictly related to the capability of the learning algorithms
               to find optimal or near-optimal solutions and to generalize to
               new examples. This chapter reviews some theoretical contributions
               to optimal learning in the attempt to provide a unified view and
               give the state of the art in the field. The focus of the review
               is on the problem of local minima in the cost function that is
