  volume   =  274,
  number   =  5293,
  pages    = "1724--1726",
  abstract = "Neurons in the cortex of behaving animals show temporally
              irregular spiking patterns. The origin of this irregularity and
              its implications for neural processing are unknown. The hypothesis
              that the temporal variability in the firing of a neuron results
              from an approximate balance between its excitatory and inhibitory
