  volume   =  17,
  number   =  1,
  pages    = "33--50",
  abstract = "We study the selective advantage of modularity in artificially
              evolved networks. Modularity abounds in complex systems in the
              real world. However, experimental evidence for the selective
              advantage of network modularity has been elusive unless it has
              been supported or mandated by the genetic representation. The
              evolutionary origin of modularity is thus still debated: whether
              networks are modular because of the process that created them, or
              the process has evolved to produce modular networks. It is
