               helps establish the validity of regression analysis when the link
               function of the regression model may be grossly wrong. A further
               generalization, which replaces $\beta'\mathbf{x}$ by
               $B'\mathbf{x}$ with $B = (\beta_1,\ldots, \beta_k)$ for $k$
               randomly selected orthonormal vectors $(\beta_i, i = 1,\ldots,
               k)$, helps broaden the scope of application of sliced inverse
               regression (SIR).",
