  journal  = "Nat. Rev. Neurosci.",
  abstract = "GABAergic inhibitory circuits play an essential role in
              coordinating various hippocampal functions. Several decades of
              work dedicated to a thorough characterization of hippocampal
              inhibitory populations have highlighted how specific types of
              interneuron can contribute to network activity. Recent studies
              have used genetically targeted recordings and peturbations of
              activity during memory-related behaviours to determine how
              interneurons that inhibit distinct subcellular domains of
              principal cells or specialize in principal cell disinhibition may
