  volume   =  5,
  number   =  2,
  pages    = "e1000291",
  abstract = "Grid cells in the rat entorhinal cortex display strikingly regular
              firing responses to the animal's position in 2-D space and have
              been hypothesized to form the neural substrate for dead-reckoning.
              However, errors accumulate rapidly when velocity inputs are
              integrated in existing models of grid cell activity. To produce
