              outcomes by delineating several fundamental and measurable
              geometric properties of neural representations that can accurately
              predict the few-shot learning performance of naturalistic concepts
              across all our numerical simulations. This theory reveals, for
              instance, that high-dimensional manifolds enhance the ability to
              learn new concepts from few examples. Intriguingly, we observe
              striking mismatches between the geometry of manifolds in the
              primate visual pathway and in trained DNNs. We discuss testable
              predictions of our theory for psychophysics and neurophysiological
              experiments.",
