              slack required to fully recognize and understand novel ideas.
              Competition among many new ideas may prevent the gradual
              accumulation of focused attention on a promising new idea. Then,
              we show data supporting the predictions of this theory. When the
              number of papers published per year in a scientific field grows
              large, citations flow disproportionately to already well-cited
              papers; the list of most-cited papers ossifies; new papers are
