              fragmentations from the first exploration of each space. Augmented
              with a long-term spatial memory and a rule similar to the
              distance-dependent Chinese Restaurant Process for selecting among
              relevant memories, the theory predicts the reuse of map fragments
              in environments with repeating substructures. Our model provides a
              simple rule for generating spatial state abstractions and predicts
              map fragmentations observed in electrophysiological recordings. It
              further predicts that there should be “fragmentation decision” or
