  journal       = "arXiv [cs.LG]",
  number        =  5,
  pages         =  054303,
  abstract      = "It has been an open question in deep learning if
                   fault-tolerant computation is possible: can arbitrarily
                   reliable computation be achieved using only unreliable
                   neurons? In the grid cells of the mammalian cortex, analog
                   error correction codes have been observed to protect states
                   against neural spiking noise, but their role in information
